id: pm-rs9vry
title: "MCP 2026-07-28 conformance programme: stateless protocol, discovery, MRTR, subscriptions, extensions, security, caching, and released-artifact proof"
description: "Migrate the pm MCP platform from the 2025-06-18 initialize-based implementation to complete 2026-07-28 conformance, with SDK-owned protocol contracts, explicit legacy compatibility, real transport tests, and release gates."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[8]: 2026-07-28,"area:mcp","area:sdk",conformance,protocol,release-gate,security,stateless
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:06:28.595Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:44:38.175Z"
deadline: "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 2400
acceptance_criteria: "The official 2026-07-28 TypeScript schema and changelog are mapped requirement by requirement to a canonical owner, implementation surface, positive test, negative test, documentation section, and release gate; Every applicable core request and result uses stateless per-request protocol metadata and the server implements mandatory discovery with deterministic capability and identity reporting; MRTR, required resultType handling, subscriptions/listen, revised tasks, caching metadata, transport headers, schema behavior, authorization rules, trace propagation, and deprecation migrations are covered by individually tracked children; Resources, prompts, tools, official extensions, and client-facing features are explicitly implemented, explicitly declared not applicable with evidence, or tracked behind a standards-based compatibility boundary; Public SDK entrypoints own protocol negotiation, validation, envelopes, capabilities, and transport-neutral behavior while CLI and MCP layers contain no private policy fork; Real-process stdio and Streamable HTTP conformance suites prove success and refusal behavior against supported and unsupported versions, malformed metadata, disconnects, retries, cache scopes, authorization issuers, and extension negotiation; Packed and published artifacts are installed and verified through npm, npx, bunx, and the MCP release probe before a release can be advertised"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make every applicable MCP 2026-07-28 core requirement and official extension reachable through SDK-owned contracts and verified over real transports
value: Agents and hosts can integrate pm through a current interoperable protocol without hand-maintained drift or legacy-session assumptions
why_now: "The shipped server advertises 2025-06-18 and requires initialize while the latest specification is stateless and changes negotiation, streaming, requests, caching, extensions, transport, and security contracts"
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: critical
confidence: high
